INT. PRINT SHOP - NIGHT #1#

A single press thumps in the dark. INES (60s), ink to the elbows, feeds it one sheet at a time.

INT. PRINT SHOP - CONTINUOUS #3#

The door opens. Theo stands in it, soaked, holding the envelope.

THEO
You said midnight.

INES
(not looking up)
I said before midnight.

She stops the press and holds out her hand. He doesn't move.

THEO
It's the only copy. [[Keep this plain. The weight is in the handover, not the line.]]

INES
Then you'll want it back.

He hands it over.

